      "writtenOn": "2024-01-06T00:12:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see the same tracking of references here as in the C version. The c version separates the (driver) internal and local (owning process) references. I don\u0027t see where this version handles all the edge cases that the C version handles without the same state information.",
      "revId": "c0bf3401d8ad68c748aa0c67ef2ed634bafbfd7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df9f9e82_6e15c487",
        "filename": "drivers/android/node.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-06T10:43:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, it\u0027s been a while since I last looked at this. I looked over the C driver, and as far as I can tell, with one exception, all uses of local/internal refs just consider the sum of local and internal refs, so most of the time, it doesn\u0027t matter which kind of reference you use. The one exception is [this check](https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/drivers/android/binder.c;l\u003d991-999;drc\u003df955e6e98c348b65772fdc1db2a9eeac3a4c3fc8). It returns an error if a remote process tries to create a strong refcount, if there are no remote processes with a strong refcount (unless its the context manager). We already have a similar check in `NodeRef::clone` and `NodeRef::update`.\n\nInterestingly,  The driver uses local references in these two cases:\n\n* Refcounts held by transactions to the target process. (Both the target node, but also nodes embedded in the transaction.)\n* Pending BR_INCREFS and BR_ACQUIRE operations.\n\nIf you change the first category of references from local to internal references, then the two drivers actually store the same information, because the number of local references is now `active_inc_refs` field.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "c8ee6931_c3e5d074",
      "revId": "c0bf3401d8ad68c748aa0c67ef2ed634bafbfd7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c632633_24a69c68",
        "filename": "drivers/android/node.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-08T17:58:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The most important difference between local and internal refs are that local refs are cleared (since they are no longer needed) when the process dies. Without that you will likely have a leak unless you have come up with a different solution to this than the C driver.",
      "parentUuid": "df9f9e82_6e15c487",
      "revId": "c0bf3401d8ad68c748aa0c67ef2ed634bafbfd7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "399980f3_b6c1af82",
        "filename": "drivers/android/node.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-09T09:45:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ultimately, the numbers tracked in the node don\u0027t control the lifetime of the node at all. That\u0027s tracked by the `Arc` pointer type that the node is wrapped in, and once all `Arc\u003cNode\u003e` references have gone out of scope, the node is deallocated even if the numbers in `NodeInner` are non-zero.\n\nIf we have a leak somewhere, then it\u0027s almost certainly due to a cycle of reference counted objects that keep each other alive. However, I\u0027ve tried to analyze the code for those in the past, and I have a piece of paper somewhere with all of the structs and arrows for the references, and I didn\u0027t find any cycles last time I did it. (Other than the cycles that `Process::deferred_release` will break, that is.)",
      "parentUuid": "5c632633_24a69c68",
      "revId": "c0bf3401d8ad68c748aa0c67ef2ed634bafbfd7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a622b57c_dcf3e42b",
        "filename": "drivers/android/node.rs",
